/T (The Multi-Armed Bandit \(MAB\) dilemma is a well-known problem in reinforcement learning. In this scenario, each arm of the slot machine gives a reward based on a particular probability distribution when activated. A single slot machine is known as a one-armed bandit, whereas multiple slot machines create a MAB or k-armed bandit, with 'k' denoting the number of slot machines present.)
